A||N||5||GML||No power at A/C compressor||||1||
Z||000000||GML||08-23-2001||01:46 PM||||I recently converted my a/c over to 134.  It took in 2 cans but the air never got cold.  I took it into a shop and they told me that I have no power going to the compressor.  Where should I look first?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-23-2001||02:14 PM||||Check the relays(1 is behind the air filter) the other up front.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GML||08-23-2001||02:20 PM||||How do I check the relay?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||08-23-2001||04:08 PM||||When my Indy did that it turned out to be the dash panel. There was a burnt place on the circuit board behind the push buttons. Put a new one in and it was ready to go!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierohoho||08-23-2001||06:19 PM||||Also, if the system has low presure the presure switch that energises the compressor will not kick in, I think, anyone?<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pennockpic.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Voytek||08-23-2001||06:27 PM||||True - if pressure is too low the compressor pressure switch will not turn it on - check the pressure.<P>Also, make sure the wires on the compressor are connected properly.<P>There is also a pressure switch up front by the receiver (silver can).  They can be faulty at times.<P>To check the compressor, you can short the two connectors on the switch up front and see if the compressor kicks in.  If it does, that means it's fine - then you have some electrical problem for sure.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
